<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / CONFIGURATION</p>
    <h1>updateconf</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Interactively process package configuration files ending in the configured
        <code>epkgnew</code> suffix under <code>/etc</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># updateconf</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="behavior">Behavior</h2>

    <p>
        The utility finds every pending new configuration file (one ending in the
        <code>epkgnew</code> suffix) under <code>/etc</code>, <code>/boot</code>,
        <code>/opt</code>, <code>/usr</code>, and <code>/var</code>. For each one it
        shows the differences against the installed file and asks you to choose:
    </p>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Key</th>
                <th>Action</th>
                <th>Effect</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>
                    <code>U</code>
                </td>

                <td>Update</td>
                <td>Replace the current file with the new version. Local changes are lost.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
                <td>
                    <code>D</code>
                </td>

                <td>Discard</td>
                <td>Delete the new file and keep the current one.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
                <td>
                    <code>E</code>
                </td>

                <td>Edit</td>
                <td>Open the current file in your editor to merge by hand, then show the diff again.</td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
                <td>
                    <code>K</code>
                </td>

                <td>Keep</td>
                <td>Leave both files; the item appears again next run.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
        A new file identical to the current one, or one whose current file does
        not exist, is removed without asking. The utility requires root access,
        uses <code>EDITOR</code> (default <code>vim</code>), and does not perform
        an automatic three-way merge.
    </p>

    <p>
        Set <code>SEARCH_DIRS</code> to limit the search, for example
        <code>SEARCH_DIRS=/etc updateconf</code>.
    </p>
</section>
